-Review and fix run in rounds. Answer every finding with a fix or, in the progress comment, a reason. Fix the finding's whole class. After the first round, review only the new diff. After three rounds, step back: reconsider the approach and ask the human before a fourth.
+Review and fix run in rounds. Answer every finding with a fix or, in the progress comment, a reason. Fix bugs, each with its whole class. Decline nits, style and cleanup findings with a one-line reason: for an agent, each one fixed is another commit and another round. A hook numbers the findings of `/code-review` and `/security-review` (F1, F2, …) and keeps the PR from being ready while one is unanswered. After the first round, review only the new diff. After three rounds, step back: reconsider the approach and ask the human before a fourth.
+
+Say what your checks would miss. When the gap reaches what the hooks decide (the gates, the guard, the halt, the archive block), run one more `/code-review xhigh` on the files behind that gap before the PR is ready. When you cannot say what they would miss, tell the human the PR needs a real review, not a quick approval.
 
 The issue is the source of truth across compaction, resumes and subagents: when memory and the issue disagree, reread the issue.
 
